      "message": "I agree that is clearer. It looks like it\u0027s slightly different though, since it adds a right shift after the left shift:\n\n arm-none-eabi-objdump -d ./build/servo_micro/RO/core/cortex-m0/task.o\n\n Disassembly of section .text.in_interrupt_context:\n\n 00000000 \u003cin_interrupt_context\u003e:\n    0:   f3ef 8005       mrs     r0, IPSR\n    4:   05c0            lsls    r0, r0, #23\n    6:   0dc0            lsrs    r0, r0, #23\n    8:   4770            bx      lr\n   \n   \nSince it looks like this is supposed to be a bool, I tried:\n\n return !!(ret \u0026 GENMASK(8, 0));\n \nwhich generates:\n\n 00000000 \u003cin_interrupt_context\u003e:\n    0:   f3ef 8005       mrs     r0, IPSR\n    4:   05c0            lsls    r0, r0, #23\n    6:   1e43            subs    r3, r0, #1\n    8:   4198            sbcs    r0, r3\n    a:   4770            bx      lr\n    \nEven though it\u0027s more instructions, I think the readability is the more important aspect.",
